From e3fa50184a28b8031805928c84cabfc63b3f67b2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: juansolo457 <5344231+Juansolo457@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 19:33:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 10/13] Aim assist: pm_AimAssist 3 finds the target anywhere in
 the aim cone

The 360 focus code (kept as pm_AimAssist 1 and 2) takes its candidates from the
clip models touching the box around the 768-unit view ray. Looking along a map
axis that box is nearly a line, so an enemy just beside the crosshair was never
a target, and the aim cone only filtered that list.

pm_AimAssist 3 searches the whole aim frustum (CONTENTS_BODY clip models in its
bounds) for the nearest living, hostile actor with a clear line from the eye.
Friction and the 360 muzzle aim then use that target. Settings > Controller >
Aim Assist gains "Full (Wide)".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
